WEBVTT

1
00:00:35,792 --> 00:00:37,208
I think we can all agree

2
00:00:37,292 --> 00:00:39,167
that things were better
under the Empire.

3
00:00:40,042 --> 00:00:43,250
Fortunately, I am still here
to protect you.

4
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:46,917
Your communities can thrive
under my protection.

5
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:50,083
You are the lucky few.

6
00:00:51,125 --> 00:00:53,458
But that which I provide
is expensive.

7
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,750
And now
I must maintain all of it

8
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,458
without the Empire's support

9
00:00:58,542 --> 00:01:00,792
until the galaxy realizes
what they've lost

10
00:01:01,542 --> 00:01:03,042
and demand our return.

11
00:01:04,375 --> 00:01:06,625
Long live the Empire.

12
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:11,500
Long live the Empire.

13
00:01:13,417 --> 00:01:14,417
Good.

14
00:01:15,458 --> 00:01:16,750
Now for the bad news.

15
00:01:18,792 --> 00:01:20,667
I am raising your tribute.

16
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:24,792
But...

17
00:01:24,875 --> 00:01:28,542
But, Your Excellency,
we are operating at a loss.

18
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:33,417
The trade routes are plagued
with pirates and thieves,

19
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,625
ready to attack at--

20
00:01:38,792 --> 00:01:41,042
Are you saying
that my protection is lacking?

21
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:43,917
No, Your Excellency.

22
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:47,875
I-I am saying that, uh--

23
00:01:52,375 --> 00:01:55,250
Perhaps you should all go
back to your townships

24
00:01:56,042 --> 00:01:57,750
and focus on solutions,

25
00:01:58,875 --> 00:02:00,292
not excuses.

26
00:02:02,292 --> 00:02:03,625
Does that sound reasonable?

27
00:02:09,208 --> 00:02:11,083
Sounds like a perimeter alarm.

28
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:13,000
I'll confirm.

29
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,750
-I've lost contact.
-Go check it.

30
00:02:20,792 --> 00:02:22,333
There's
nothing to worry about.

31
00:02:22,417 --> 00:02:24,667
I'll send for reinforcements.

32
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,875
I will require
a revenue projection...

33
00:02:53,625 --> 00:02:55,667
We need backup. On the double!

34
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:56,750
Code Red.

35
00:03:04,042 --> 00:03:05,125
Lay down cover fire.

36
00:03:07,417 --> 00:03:08,667
Take up arms!

37
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:24,417
Long live the Empire!

38
00:05:07,792 --> 00:05:10,000
What are you waiting for?
Hop on.

39
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,667
Hang on.

40
00:05:54,292 --> 00:05:55,292
Did we get him?

41
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:56,792
Not yet, sir.
But we will.

42
00:06:05,042 --> 00:06:07,708
- We missed him! He's under us.
- We have him.

43
00:06:07,792 --> 00:06:08,792
Fire.

44
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:55,917
What's going on?
Give me a status report.

45
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,542
Has the target
been eliminated?

46
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:59,833
- We've lost contact.
- Walker Three is gone.

47
00:07:00,458 --> 00:07:02,667
- Send everybody!
- Understood.

48
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:03,958
Prepare to engage!

49
00:07:12,833 --> 00:07:13,917
Get ready. Weapons up.

50
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,500
Full barrel. Now, let's go.

51
00:07:50,542 --> 00:07:52,208
Give me a status update.

52
00:07:52,292 --> 00:07:54,542
Did you see him?
Have you located him?

53
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,208
Did you get The Mandalorian?

54
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:00,458
Something's up there.

55
00:08:02,625 --> 00:08:03,958
He's on the roof!

56
00:08:04,625 --> 00:08:05,625
Can you see him?

57
00:08:06,292 --> 00:08:07,292
Take him out!

58
00:08:07,375 --> 00:08:08,375
Get up there.

59
00:08:09,167 --> 00:08:10,292
But we're pilots.

60
00:08:10,375 --> 00:08:13,083
-Go now! Do it!
-Yes, sir. On our way.

61
00:08:13,167 --> 00:08:14,500
Get up there.

62
00:08:15,667 --> 00:08:16,667
Set the charges.

63
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:18,167
-Prepare for exfil.
-Sir.

64
00:08:18,250 --> 00:08:21,625
He's breaching the hatch.
He's breaching the hatch!

65
00:08:39,375 --> 00:08:40,375
Autopilot.

66
00:09:13,292 --> 00:09:15,208
I know, I know.
I need to get the shot.

67
00:09:45,292 --> 00:09:47,958
You know, it's better
if you bring 'em in alive.

68
00:09:55,042 --> 00:09:56,042
You okay?

69
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:00,875
You see, you catch the bad guy

70
00:10:00,958 --> 00:10:03,333
and they tell us
where the other bad guys are.

71
00:10:04,042 --> 00:10:05,792
Things went a little sideways.

72
00:12:26,667 --> 00:12:29,458
Good luck.
You're gonna need it.

73
00:12:37,958 --> 00:12:40,625
Messy. Very messy.

74
00:12:41,917 --> 00:12:44,542
It was the best I could do
under the circumstances.

75
00:12:45,542 --> 00:12:47,542
The problem is,
we need information.

76
00:12:48,417 --> 00:12:50,250
Without it, we're never gonna
get to the bottom of

77
00:12:50,333 --> 00:12:52,167
what the Empire's up to.

78
00:12:52,250 --> 00:12:53,250
Just give me time,

79
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:55,833
I'll take out every bad guy
in your deck of cards.

80
00:12:55,917 --> 00:12:57,458
This isn't about revenge.

81
00:12:57,958 --> 00:13:00,583
It's about
preventing another war...

82
00:13:03,833 --> 00:13:06,500
...and protecting everything
the Rebellion fought for.

83
00:13:06,583 --> 00:13:08,792
Does that mean I'm not
getting paid for this one?

84
00:13:10,583 --> 00:13:12,417
You're getting paid all right.

85
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,500
Come with me.

86
00:13:22,833 --> 00:13:24,042
Impressive.

87
00:13:24,125 --> 00:13:25,458
Where did you get
one of these?

88
00:13:26,167 --> 00:13:28,292
It was from
a captured Imperial commandant

89
00:13:28,375 --> 00:13:30,625
who had a big collection
of vintage vehicles.

90
00:13:31,125 --> 00:13:33,750
This one is stock.
Perfectly restored.

91
00:13:34,417 --> 00:13:36,125
I took it out for a test spin.

92
00:13:36,708 --> 00:13:38,625
They did a nice job
on the rebuild.

93
00:13:41,333 --> 00:13:43,042
This is worth a lot more than

94
00:13:43,125 --> 00:13:44,625
the bounty on that Imp.

95
00:13:44,708 --> 00:13:47,333
Well, let's call it an advance
on the next mission.

96
00:13:49,583 --> 00:13:50,708
What next mission?

97
00:13:51,375 --> 00:13:52,833
Commander Coin.

98
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,333
Our missing Ace of Staves.

99
00:13:57,750 --> 00:13:59,417
No one knows
what he looks like

100
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,542
and most
believe him to be dead.

101
00:14:02,250 --> 00:14:05,000
Not a lot to go on.
What's the play?

102
00:14:05,083 --> 00:14:08,250
I want you to go to Nal Hutta
and meet with the Hutts.

103
00:14:08,833 --> 00:14:10,792
They've agreed to
lead us to him.

104
00:14:10,875 --> 00:14:11,875
What's in it for them?

105
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,833
Their nephew's being held
against his will

106
00:14:14,917 --> 00:14:17,417
by another crime syndicate
on the Outer Rim,

107
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:18,708
and they need a professional

108
00:14:18,792 --> 00:14:20,375
to get him out
quickly and quietly.

109
00:14:20,458 --> 00:14:21,458
Where is he?

110
00:14:21,958 --> 00:14:23,417
They'll only tell you
in person.

111
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:25,250
You got a name?

112
00:14:25,958 --> 00:14:27,583
His name is Rotta the Hutt.

113
00:14:27,667 --> 00:14:31,083
The only surviving heir
of crime lord Jabba the Hutt.

114
00:14:31,667 --> 00:14:32,917
You ever cross his path?

115
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,625
I tried not to.

116
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:36,833
So...

117
00:14:37,708 --> 00:14:38,833
do we have a deal?

118
00:14:38,917 --> 00:14:41,292
I only hunt down
Imperial war criminals.

119
00:14:41,375 --> 00:14:44,833
I don't work for gangsters
anymore, especially the Hutts.

120
00:14:44,917 --> 00:14:47,417
That's right, you don't.
You work for us.

121
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:50,333
And right now, this is
what we need you to do.

122
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,958
You don't want the job,
I got nothing for you.

123
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:06,792
Come aboard.

124
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,833
May as well
have a look around.

125
00:15:15,792 --> 00:15:17,333
Let's go hear the Hutts out.

126
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:19,958
I'll even let you fly
this time.

127
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,417
I didn't say yes.

128
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,167
You didn't say no either.

129
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:48,667
She's stock, but she's clean.

130
00:16:05,542 --> 00:16:07,292
Hey.

131
00:16:07,375 --> 00:16:08,583
Don't touch anything.

132
00:16:09,125 --> 00:16:10,458
Never touch the buttons.

133
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:56,167
Identify yourself.

134
00:17:57,458 --> 00:17:59,917
Razor Crest,
requesting clearance.

135
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
I'm here
by invitation of the Twins.

136
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,333
Easy on the sticks.
They're expecting us.

137
00:18:07,042 --> 00:18:08,292
We should be fine.

138
00:18:10,708 --> 00:18:12,417
Clearance granted.

139
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,875
You are clear to approach.

140
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:16,750
They've got
a lot of firepower here.

141
00:18:16,833 --> 00:18:19,958
Yeah. Looks like
they hired the Droid Gotra.

142
00:18:20,042 --> 00:18:22,042
The Hutts
take security seriously.

143
00:19:13,125 --> 00:19:14,958
The Hutts have been the
head of criminal enterprises

144
00:19:15,042 --> 00:19:16,583
for thousands of years.

145
00:19:21,083 --> 00:19:23,042
They use
violence and treachery

146
00:19:23,125 --> 00:19:24,333
to maintain control.

147
00:19:26,083 --> 00:19:27,458
Be careful.

148
00:19:27,542 --> 00:19:32,125
We may be their guests,
but we are not safe.

149
00:20:16,125 --> 00:20:19,375
We finally meet the legendary Mandalorian.

150
00:20:20,583 --> 00:20:25,000
We are so glad you agreed to work for us.

151
00:20:25,583 --> 00:20:27,833
You will be very rich.

152
00:20:27,917 --> 00:20:29,458
I don't work for you.

153
00:20:29,542 --> 00:20:31,042
I work for the New Republic.

154
00:20:31,917 --> 00:20:33,000
I'm told you can lead us

155
00:20:33,083 --> 00:20:35,375
to the Imperial fugitive
Commander Coin.

156
00:20:36,250 --> 00:20:38,500
Of course, Mando.

157
00:20:38,583 --> 00:20:40,333
I understand
your nephew, Rotta,

158
00:20:40,417 --> 00:20:41,708
has been kidnapped.

159
00:20:42,042 --> 00:20:45,083
Yes, our poor nephew has been taken.

160
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,625
He fell in with a bad crowd.

161
00:20:49,042 --> 00:20:51,708
We are heartbroken.

162
00:20:52,458 --> 00:20:55,208
Think of how you would feel

163
00:20:55,292 --> 00:20:58,375
if your little one went missing.

164
00:21:00,667 --> 00:21:02,167
What does he look like?

165
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:03,458
Do you have an image?

166
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:05,083
Ah, yes.

167
00:21:05,583 --> 00:21:09,375
The only image we have is from long ago.

168
00:21:15,958 --> 00:21:19,667
He's had a growth spurt since then.

169
00:21:20,417 --> 00:21:24,000
Okay.
I'll rescue your nephew.

170
00:21:24,083 --> 00:21:25,083
Where is he being held?

171
00:21:25,750 --> 00:21:30,667
You will find him on the moon of Shakari.

172
00:21:31,250 --> 00:21:32,667
It shall be done.

173
00:21:52,167 --> 00:21:53,917
We're about to
come out of hyperspace

174
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,333
in the Shakari system.

175
00:21:55,958 --> 00:21:58,125
To state
the obvious, you are operating

176
00:21:58,208 --> 00:22:00,375
outside the jurisdiction
of the New Republic.

177
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:05,375
If things get messy, I can't
call in an X-wing strike.

178
00:22:05,917 --> 00:22:07,792
I know the drill.

179
00:22:08,667 --> 00:22:12,292
Before going into harm's way,
check your armor first.

180
00:22:12,375 --> 00:22:14,833
It's gotta fit snug
so it doesn't slide,

181
00:22:14,917 --> 00:22:17,542
but not so tight that it
restricts your movement.

182
00:22:18,250 --> 00:22:19,417
Got it?

183
00:22:20,917 --> 00:22:22,417
How's that feel?

184
00:22:46,125 --> 00:22:47,917
All right, Zeb, drop us here.

185
00:23:44,500 --> 00:23:45,500
Yes?

186
00:23:45,583 --> 00:23:47,333
I'll take a flat-meat fry
for the little one.

187
00:23:47,417 --> 00:23:49,125
Got it. Okay, got it, got it.

188
00:23:49,208 --> 00:23:50,667
Flat-meat fry, huh?

189
00:23:53,208 --> 00:23:54,792
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

190
00:24:01,042 --> 00:24:02,333
Whoa.

191
00:24:02,417 --> 00:24:04,083
That's quite an
impressive denomination.

192
00:24:04,167 --> 00:24:05,542
I'm not sure I've got
change for that.

193
00:24:05,625 --> 00:24:06,958
You can keep the change.

194
00:24:07,042 --> 00:24:08,667
I'm new to these parts.

195
00:24:08,750 --> 00:24:10,875
I can use some information.

196
00:24:10,958 --> 00:24:13,333
Yeah, for this price, I'll
tell you whatever you want.

197
00:24:13,833 --> 00:24:15,250
I'm looking for a Hutt.

198
00:24:15,333 --> 00:24:17,833
Shh. Don't mention that name.
Don't say that.

199
00:24:17,917 --> 00:24:19,333
What, are you trying
to get us both killed?

200
00:24:19,417 --> 00:24:21,500
Here. Keep your credits.
Food's on me.

201
00:24:22,042 --> 00:24:23,833
Go away. Thank you.

202
00:24:23,917 --> 00:24:26,500
Okay, never happened.
Let's go. Nothing to see here.

203
00:24:26,583 --> 00:24:28,167
Damn Mandalorian,
talking like that.

204
00:24:28,250 --> 00:24:30,500
Just out in the open,
he talks like... What is this?

205
00:24:30,583 --> 00:24:33,250
No, no, no. No, no, no, no.
I don't want your credits,

206
00:24:33,333 --> 00:24:34,750
'cause I didn't give you
any information.

207
00:24:34,833 --> 00:24:36,250
His name is Rotta.

208
00:24:37,125 --> 00:24:38,125
Really?

209
00:24:40,417 --> 00:24:41,667
Something funny?

210
00:24:41,750 --> 00:24:43,208
Yeah, yeah.
Everybody...

211
00:24:43,292 --> 00:24:45,125
Everybody knows
Rotta the Hutt.

212
00:24:45,208 --> 00:24:47,333
That guy's a monster.

213
00:25:33,583 --> 00:25:34,958
Rotta! Rotta! Rotta!

214
00:25:35,042 --> 00:25:37,208
He doesn't seem like
a prisoner to me.

215
00:25:39,292 --> 00:25:40,958
...Rotta!

216
00:26:21,208 --> 00:26:22,750
Are you here to kill me?

217
00:26:23,625 --> 00:26:25,333
I'm here to rescue you.

218
00:26:27,458 --> 00:26:29,833
What makes you think
I need rescuing?

219
00:26:29,917 --> 00:26:31,792
Your aunt and uncle
hired me to find you.

220
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:37,000
Yeah, I see. Well, thank you,
but I don't require rescuing.

221
00:26:37,625 --> 00:26:40,042
Tomorrow's the last match
in my contract and after that,

222
00:26:40,125 --> 00:26:41,833
my debt will be paid.

223
00:26:41,917 --> 00:26:43,583
I'll be a free agent.

224
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:48,333
Paid to who?

225
00:26:51,167 --> 00:26:52,167
Who's he?

226
00:26:53,292 --> 00:26:55,125
Don't stare.

227
00:26:55,208 --> 00:26:57,167
It's okay. What's your name?

228
00:26:57,250 --> 00:26:59,208
He doesn't talk.

229
00:26:59,292 --> 00:27:00,917
Who do you have to pay?

230
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,375
Can I feed him?

231
00:27:06,375 --> 00:27:07,583
Sure.

232
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:09,083
Who do you have to pay?

233
00:27:14,875 --> 00:27:16,292
Lord Janu.

234
00:27:17,667 --> 00:27:19,250
I don't know the name.

235
00:27:19,333 --> 00:27:20,708
You should.

236
00:27:20,792 --> 00:27:23,542
He runs the Syndicate
on all the moons of Shakari.

237
00:27:26,167 --> 00:27:27,583
He signed me to his stable.

238
00:27:27,667 --> 00:27:29,833
He bankrolled
my board and training.

239
00:27:29,917 --> 00:27:31,792
He keeps you in a cage.

240
00:27:31,875 --> 00:27:33,000
He treats me well.

241
00:27:33,542 --> 00:27:36,333
And after tomorrow night,
I'll be my own man.

242
00:27:36,417 --> 00:27:39,000
And with the following
he got me as a promoter,

243
00:27:39,083 --> 00:27:41,167
not only will my debt be paid,

244
00:27:41,250 --> 00:27:42,750
but I'll be rich
by the solstice.

245
00:27:42,833 --> 00:27:44,958
Grogu, heel!

246
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:50,250
Don't worry,
I'm not my father.

247
00:27:55,708 --> 00:27:58,083
You know how hard it is
to be your own man

248
00:27:58,167 --> 00:28:00,042
when your father is
Jabba the Hutt?

249
00:28:05,667 --> 00:28:08,083
You see them
cheering for me out there?

250
00:28:08,167 --> 00:28:09,167
For me.

251
00:28:09,917 --> 00:28:13,125
It's the first time
I'm not living in his shadow.

252
00:28:13,208 --> 00:28:15,250
That's why
I fight in the pits.

253
00:28:15,750 --> 00:28:19,042
They feared him,
but they cheer for me.

254
00:28:20,833 --> 00:28:22,083
So, no...

255
00:28:22,792 --> 00:28:24,667
I don't need to be rescued.

256
00:28:28,667 --> 00:28:30,417
Where can I find Lord Janu?

257
00:28:32,125 --> 00:28:34,000
Thank you.
Closed for the night.

258
00:28:38,833 --> 00:28:41,000
What the hell's he thinking?
Damn Mandalorians.

259
00:28:41,083 --> 00:28:42,667
Mandalorians, they don't even
come from here.

260
00:28:42,750 --> 00:28:44,333
He's going around, talking--

261
00:28:45,583 --> 00:28:48,583
I just wanna know
where I can find Lord Janu.

262
00:28:48,667 --> 00:28:51,917
Don't say that.
Do not say that name.

263
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,542
Stop saying it.

264
00:28:53,625 --> 00:28:55,750
I recommend you calm down.

265
00:28:56,292 --> 00:28:57,917
Just, please, please,
don't kill me. Don't kill me.

266
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,833
I've got... I've got
12 little ones at home,

267
00:28:59,917 --> 00:29:01,958
smaller than him.
It's... They're smaller.

268
00:29:02,792 --> 00:29:04,750
Yeah, it's just...

269
00:29:04,833 --> 00:29:07,208
I pay him protection, okay?

270
00:29:07,292 --> 00:29:08,292
We all do.

271
00:29:08,375 --> 00:29:09,917
I barely make a living,
to be honest.

272
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,417
-But at least I'm alive.
-Who collects for him?

273
00:29:12,500 --> 00:29:14,167
I don't know.
Different people come in.

274
00:29:14,250 --> 00:29:16,333
Sometimes they come here,
sometimes I do a drop myself.

275
00:29:16,417 --> 00:29:17,958
-What do I know?
-Where?

276
00:29:18,042 --> 00:29:20,750
-Where what?
-Where do you do the drops?

277
00:29:20,833 --> 00:29:22,208
I don't... Some pla...
Sometimes,

278
00:29:22,292 --> 00:29:24,208
I go down to...
...different places.

279
00:29:24,292 --> 00:29:26,250
Usually... Sometimes
I go to the salt bar

280
00:29:26,333 --> 00:29:28,125
under Korvin Station.

281
00:29:28,208 --> 00:29:30,167
And then there's
other places too. You go to...

282
00:29:30,250 --> 00:29:31,917
You know. You know,
I go around.

283
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:35,375
No, I don't want it.
I don't want it.

284
00:29:35,458 --> 00:29:36,833
I didn't give you
any information.

285
00:29:36,917 --> 00:29:38,667
-I was just talking.
-That's not for information.

286
00:29:39,208 --> 00:29:40,417
It's to cover his tab.

287
00:30:26,250 --> 00:30:27,750
I'm looking for Lord Janu.

288
00:30:32,375 --> 00:30:34,292
Maybe you made a mistake.

289
00:30:36,250 --> 00:30:38,917
Maybe you remember wrong
and think you know me.

290
00:30:42,458 --> 00:30:44,667
Maybe you just walked through
the wrong door.

291
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:48,375
Well,
I'm not here to buy salt.

292
00:30:49,167 --> 00:30:50,375
Salt?

293
00:30:51,208 --> 00:30:52,583
We don't sell salt.

294
00:30:53,500 --> 00:30:54,625
It's on the ration.

295
00:30:57,083 --> 00:30:59,083
How much
for the shoulder candy?

296
00:31:01,958 --> 00:31:03,833
Would look real pretty
in a cage.

297
00:31:04,917 --> 00:31:06,583
I'm here to see Lord Janu.

298
00:31:07,875 --> 00:31:09,958
I won't repeat myself again.

299
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:01,042
It seems you've
earned your salt today.

300
00:32:04,208 --> 00:32:05,250
I'm Janu.

301
00:32:06,333 --> 00:32:08,292
Come to the back
and pick out a crystal.

302
00:32:08,792 --> 00:32:09,792
Hogsbreth,

303
00:32:11,625 --> 00:32:13,167
have the boys clean up.

304
00:32:14,458 --> 00:32:16,583
Make sure
I don't lose any pets.

305
00:32:35,250 --> 00:32:36,250
Here.

306
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:38,167
Choose one.

307
00:32:38,250 --> 00:32:40,875
Salt is of no value to me
where I'm from.

308
00:32:40,958 --> 00:32:42,958
But here
it's worth a small fortune,

309
00:32:43,042 --> 00:32:46,292
because it's rationed
by the politicians.

310
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,500
Which makes it rare.

311
00:32:49,958 --> 00:32:51,625
As are you, Mandalorian.

312
00:32:53,208 --> 00:32:55,292
Have you ever considered
fighting in the pits?

313
00:32:55,375 --> 00:32:57,375
I try to avoid violence.

314
00:32:58,792 --> 00:33:00,000
'Course you do.

315
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:02,208
I do as well.

316
00:33:04,042 --> 00:33:05,708
So what brings you to
this establishment

317
00:33:05,792 --> 00:33:07,375
if you're not
in the market for salt?

318
00:33:07,458 --> 00:33:10,417
I wanna buy out the contract
on a fighter from your stable.

319
00:33:11,042 --> 00:33:13,708
Perhaps you would consider
joining my stable instead?

320
00:33:19,875 --> 00:33:22,417
This buys a lot of salt
where I'm from.

321
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:23,667
I am offering you this

322
00:33:23,750 --> 00:33:26,542
in exchange for the fighting
contract on Rotta the Hutt.

323
00:33:26,625 --> 00:33:28,667
My dear boy,
there's no price high enough

324
00:33:28,750 --> 00:33:30,875
to buy him out of
his last fights.

325
00:33:30,958 --> 00:33:33,167
I've been grooming that
little prince for many cycles,

326
00:33:33,250 --> 00:33:34,875
setting him up
for tomorrow's match.

327
00:33:34,958 --> 00:33:36,000
Take the credits.

328
00:33:36,083 --> 00:33:38,292
It's his last fight
for you anyway.

329
00:33:39,417 --> 00:33:40,667
It's his last fight ever.

330
00:33:42,292 --> 00:33:43,750
I've collected
the most deadly creatures

331
00:33:43,833 --> 00:33:45,333
from across the galaxy.

332
00:33:45,875 --> 00:33:47,833
He's fighting a Dejarik match?

333
00:33:48,375 --> 00:33:49,500
Yes.

334
00:33:50,208 --> 00:33:51,792
He will die tomorrow.

335
00:33:52,958 --> 00:33:54,458
And a select few know it.

336
00:33:55,333 --> 00:33:56,667
Here's my gift to you:

337
00:33:57,708 --> 00:33:58,708
take those credits,

338
00:34:00,167 --> 00:34:02,000
bet it all
on the death of the Hutt.

339
00:34:02,875 --> 00:34:04,292
In exchange,

340
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:07,917
all I ask is that you
consider fighting in my pit.

341
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,167
The people of Shakari
would pay any price

342
00:34:10,250 --> 00:34:12,125
to see the rarest of sights,

343
00:34:12,208 --> 00:34:15,000
one of the legendary
Mandalorian warriors

344
00:34:15,083 --> 00:34:17,458
engaging in blood sport.

345
00:34:26,125 --> 00:34:27,542
This should more than cover

346
00:34:28,125 --> 00:34:30,083
our little misunderstanding
out there.

347
00:34:34,042 --> 00:34:36,167
All I ask
is that you consider my offer.

348
00:34:37,875 --> 00:34:40,167
Could make us both very rich.

349
00:35:14,458 --> 00:35:17,292
Looks like we're gonna have to
do this the hard way.

350
00:36:46,042 --> 00:36:47,417
What?

351
00:36:48,458 --> 00:36:50,042
Janu's planning on
killing you.

352
00:36:50,125 --> 00:36:51,250
I'm here to get you out.

353
00:36:54,583 --> 00:36:57,500
Tomorrow's my last fight.
I'll be free after I win.

354
00:36:57,583 --> 00:37:00,958
The fix is in.
It's a Dejarik match.

355
00:37:01,042 --> 00:37:02,708
He will keep
throwing opponents at you

356
00:37:02,792 --> 00:37:03,875
until you die.

357
00:37:03,958 --> 00:37:05,708
Why should I believe you?

358
00:37:06,208 --> 00:37:08,542
You were sent by my aunt
and uncle who want me dead.

359
00:37:08,625 --> 00:37:10,250
They want you back.

360
00:37:10,333 --> 00:37:11,792
You're embarrassing them.

361
00:37:11,875 --> 00:37:12,958
The Twins want me dead

362
00:37:13,042 --> 00:37:15,625
because I'm heir
to the throne, not them.

363
00:37:15,708 --> 00:37:17,250
But I don't want it.

364
00:37:17,333 --> 00:37:19,708
I don't wanna be anything
like my father.

365
00:37:20,750 --> 00:37:23,833
When I first started fighting,
the people all booed me.

366
00:37:23,917 --> 00:37:25,375
They wanted to see me die

367
00:37:25,458 --> 00:37:27,542
because I'm the son
of Jabba the Hutt.

368
00:37:27,625 --> 00:37:29,417
Then I won
and became a champion

369
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:31,583
and they slowly
began to cheer.

370
00:37:31,667 --> 00:37:33,667
They realized
I'm not my father.

371
00:37:33,750 --> 00:37:35,167
I'm my own man,

372
00:37:35,250 --> 00:37:37,583
and I'm not afraid to fight
for what I have.

373
00:37:37,667 --> 00:37:40,500
To earn it.
To prove myself to everyone.

374
00:37:41,417 --> 00:37:44,042
Kid, fighting's not a sport.

375
00:37:44,125 --> 00:37:45,958
It's a last resort.

376
00:37:46,042 --> 00:37:48,125
Now come with me
before things get ugly.

377
00:37:48,208 --> 00:37:50,542
Guards, he's back!

378
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Get out. Get out!

379
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:44,292
Rotta! Rotta! Rotta!

380
00:39:04,333 --> 00:39:06,250
Rotta!

381
00:39:33,333 --> 00:39:34,750
I don't want to fight you.

382
00:39:35,667 --> 00:39:37,708
Then you're in for a long day!

383
00:39:47,167 --> 00:39:48,208
Yes!

384
00:40:13,792 --> 00:40:16,542
I'm not going to kill you.

385
00:40:16,625 --> 00:40:18,333
I'm here to rescue you.

386
00:41:05,083 --> 00:41:12,875
Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill!

387
00:41:12,958 --> 00:41:15,750
Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill!

388
00:41:15,833 --> 00:41:18,208
Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill!

389
00:41:18,292 --> 00:41:20,042
Kill! Kill! Kill...

390
00:41:20,125 --> 00:41:21,292
I yield.

391
00:41:25,875 --> 00:41:27,958
Rotta the Hutt has won.

392
00:41:28,042 --> 00:41:30,708
Now you owe him his freedom.

393
00:41:37,750 --> 00:41:39,833
Rotta the Hutt has won.

394
00:41:40,583 --> 00:41:42,500
Now he is free...

395
00:41:45,167 --> 00:41:46,292
to die!

396
00:42:32,042 --> 00:42:34,833
Our only chance
is to work together.

397
00:43:59,042 --> 00:44:00,792
Watch out for the little one.

398
00:44:00,875 --> 00:44:02,167
Yeah, I got this.

399
00:45:13,250 --> 00:45:14,250
We should go now.

400
00:45:14,333 --> 00:45:15,500
Now!

401
00:45:45,792 --> 00:45:46,792
Are you good?

402
00:45:48,292 --> 00:45:50,708
Don't worry, buddy.
We're getting out of here.

403
00:46:13,625 --> 00:46:15,833
You were right.
The fix was in.

404
00:46:15,917 --> 00:46:17,375
Let's get you out of here.

405
00:46:19,125 --> 00:46:20,750
I'm gonna find us a ride.

406
00:46:43,042 --> 00:46:44,292
Sorry, Mando.

407
00:46:44,375 --> 00:46:45,833
I can't go back.

408
00:47:09,208 --> 00:47:11,042
Zeb, I got a runner.

409
00:48:01,500 --> 00:48:03,708
Okay, you got me.

410
00:48:04,750 --> 00:48:06,667
Can't blame a guy for trying.

411
00:48:24,667 --> 00:48:26,875
We're about
to jump to hyperspace.

412
00:48:26,958 --> 00:48:28,375
Where are you bringing me?

413
00:48:28,458 --> 00:48:30,208
It's not safe
to keep you chained up.

414
00:48:30,708 --> 00:48:31,917
If I unlock you,

415
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:33,958
can we agree
to no funny stuff?

416
00:48:34,042 --> 00:48:36,083
Are you bringing me
to Nal Hutta?

417
00:48:36,167 --> 00:48:37,250
This is an old ship.

418
00:48:37,333 --> 00:48:39,250
Sometimes things
get a little bouncy.

419
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:42,125
My aunt and uncle
were scared of my father.

420
00:48:42,208 --> 00:48:44,208
They've always
been cruel to me.

421
00:48:44,292 --> 00:48:46,417
Now that they control
his criminal empire,

422
00:48:46,500 --> 00:48:48,167
they need me eliminated.

423
00:48:48,250 --> 00:48:50,333
You bring me to them,
I'm a dead man.

424
00:48:50,417 --> 00:48:51,458
You don't know that.

425
00:48:51,542 --> 00:48:52,625
If you let me go,

426
00:48:52,708 --> 00:48:54,458
you'll never
hear from me again.

427
00:48:54,958 --> 00:48:56,625
It's a big galaxy.

428
00:48:56,708 --> 00:48:57,917
I can disappear.

429
00:48:58,000 --> 00:48:59,667
Sorry, kid.

430
00:48:59,750 --> 00:49:01,333
I was hired to do a job.

431
00:49:01,917 --> 00:49:04,125
I don't know how
you sleep at night,

432
00:49:04,208 --> 00:49:05,792
working for those monsters.

433
00:49:06,333 --> 00:49:08,167
I don't work for them,

434
00:49:08,250 --> 00:49:10,292
I work for the New Republic.

435
00:49:10,375 --> 00:49:12,792
They hired me, not the Twins.

436
00:49:13,292 --> 00:49:14,917
When I bring you back,
they're giving me

437
00:49:15,000 --> 00:49:16,708
the whereabouts
of Commander Coin,

438
00:49:16,792 --> 00:49:19,750
a high-ranking ex-Imperial
operating on the Outer Rim.

439
00:49:20,250 --> 00:49:21,542
It's Janu.

440
00:49:22,667 --> 00:49:25,542
The man you're looking for
is Janu.

441
00:49:25,625 --> 00:49:27,000
Lord Janu Coin.

442
00:49:27,500 --> 00:49:28,958
That's who the Hutts
are gonna give you.

443
00:49:29,042 --> 00:49:30,333
He's ex-Imperial.

444
00:49:30,417 --> 00:49:32,750
That can't be.
The Twins would've told me.

445
00:49:32,833 --> 00:49:34,458
I saw stormtroopers.

446
00:49:35,375 --> 00:49:37,000
He brought me
to his estate once

447
00:49:37,083 --> 00:49:38,167
to celebrate a big win

448
00:49:38,250 --> 00:49:40,500
and there were
stormtroopers everywhere.

449
00:49:40,583 --> 00:49:42,542
If you don't believe me
and you don't get him now,

450
00:49:42,625 --> 00:49:44,042
you won't get another shot.

451
00:49:44,542 --> 00:49:46,208
In fact,
it might already be too late.

452
00:49:47,083 --> 00:49:48,625
That's quite a story.

453
00:49:48,708 --> 00:49:50,417
Why should I believe you?

454
00:49:50,500 --> 00:49:53,542
You're a bounty hunter,
you know when someone's lying.

455
00:49:55,917 --> 00:49:57,500
Am I lying...

456
00:49:57,583 --> 00:49:59,250
or am I telling the truth?

457
00:50:19,958 --> 00:50:21,083
That's it.

458
00:50:21,667 --> 00:50:23,583
That's Janu Coin's compound.

459
00:50:24,417 --> 00:50:27,000
Could be big boy's
telling the truth.

460
00:50:27,083 --> 00:50:29,750
The place is lousy
with stormtroopers.

461
00:50:33,208 --> 00:50:34,417
How many did you see

462
00:50:34,500 --> 00:50:35,500
when you were in there?

463
00:50:36,458 --> 00:50:37,458
A lot.

464
00:50:38,542 --> 00:50:39,875
You're gonna need
a lot of backup

465
00:50:39,958 --> 00:50:41,792
if you're actually
thinking of going in.

466
00:50:42,708 --> 00:50:43,833
Uh-huh.

467
00:50:45,125 --> 00:50:47,083
Get word
to all our foot soldiers

468
00:50:47,167 --> 00:50:49,083
on the dark side of Shakari.

469
00:50:49,167 --> 00:50:52,833
I want eyes on the starport
and all the freight lanes.

470
00:50:52,917 --> 00:50:53,917
Lean on the mayor.

471
00:50:54,000 --> 00:50:56,250
Nothing takes off
or lands until we find them.

472
00:50:56,333 --> 00:50:58,417
Muster
my personal security forces.

473
00:50:59,042 --> 00:51:01,250
We're going to hit the streets
in full armor.

474
00:51:01,333 --> 00:51:02,583
I don't want to
take any chances

475
00:51:02,667 --> 00:51:04,042
when it comes to
The Mandalorian.

476
00:51:04,125 --> 00:51:06,417
I've heard many things
about those monsters.

477
00:51:06,917 --> 00:51:08,250
It's all true.

478
00:51:09,750 --> 00:51:11,917
Imperial Commander Janu Coin,

479
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:13,750
I'm here on behalf
of the New Republic

480
00:51:13,833 --> 00:51:15,375
to bring you to justice.

481
00:51:16,000 --> 00:51:18,500
I'm afraid we're outside
of your jurisdiction.

482
00:51:19,250 --> 00:51:20,542
Take him!

483
00:51:25,375 --> 00:51:26,958
-Set blasters on full.
-Hurry!

484
00:52:26,250 --> 00:52:28,083
I can bring you in warm...

485
00:52:29,667 --> 00:52:31,583
or I can bring you in cold.

486
00:52:55,583 --> 00:52:56,958
Grogu.

487
00:52:58,500 --> 00:52:59,625
Rotta.

488
00:53:00,333 --> 00:53:01,792
Rotta, come in.

489
00:53:01,875 --> 00:53:03,250
Does anyone read me?

490
00:53:04,833 --> 00:53:06,042
I'm up. I'm up.

491
00:53:06,125 --> 00:53:08,292
I need you
to fire up the drives.

492
00:53:08,375 --> 00:53:09,458
Fire up the drives.

493
00:53:09,542 --> 00:53:11,292
-We have company.
-Received.

494
00:53:12,042 --> 00:53:14,375
I don't know how to fly.
Do you know how to fly?

495
00:53:15,167 --> 00:53:16,833
Neither of us know how to fly,

496
00:53:16,917 --> 00:53:18,625
and I can't even
fit in the cockpit.

497
00:53:25,125 --> 00:53:28,500
Grogu, I need you to go
to the control panel.

498
00:53:28,583 --> 00:53:30,583
Remember the buttons
I told you never to touch?

499
00:53:30,667 --> 00:53:32,292
I'm gonna need you
to touch them.

500
00:53:32,375 --> 00:53:35,125
Look for
the ignition relay cutoff.

501
00:53:35,208 --> 00:53:37,333
It's next to
the fuel differential readout,

502
00:53:37,875 --> 00:53:40,667
which is between
the pump compression gauge

503
00:53:40,750 --> 00:53:42,542
and the primary
reserve indic--

504
00:53:45,125 --> 00:53:46,542
Whoa.

505
00:53:46,625 --> 00:53:49,125
No. Don't touch
the missile battery switch.

506
00:53:49,208 --> 00:53:50,833
That's why there's
a safety guard on it.

507
00:53:50,917 --> 00:53:53,042
Do you see
the fuel readout display?

508
00:53:53,125 --> 00:53:54,583
Remember
I showed you that one?

509
00:53:54,667 --> 00:53:55,833
It's on the other side

510
00:53:55,917 --> 00:53:58,250
of the manual control
surface calibration un--

511
00:54:00,958 --> 00:54:02,833
I don't think
he knows what he's doing.

512
00:54:25,208 --> 00:54:26,333
Get out.

513
00:54:30,875 --> 00:54:33,375
Get going.
They're shooting at you too.

514
00:54:41,750 --> 00:54:43,708
Good job, buddy. Strap in.

515
00:55:08,375 --> 00:55:09,917
I like this kid.

516
00:55:20,583 --> 00:55:22,417
Come on. Come on.

517
00:55:34,667 --> 00:55:36,542
Get us out of atmosphere
and jump!

518
00:55:36,625 --> 00:55:37,667
Get up here.

519
00:55:37,750 --> 00:55:39,750
I need you to bypass
the exhaust restrictors.

520
00:55:53,583 --> 00:55:56,000
This old junker's
gonna get us killed.

521
00:55:56,083 --> 00:55:57,208
I need more power.

522
00:55:57,292 --> 00:55:59,958
Disable the safety panel
so I can override the limiter.

523
00:56:00,042 --> 00:56:02,708
How? I'm a pilot,
not a meknek.

524
00:56:02,792 --> 00:56:04,917
Just rip out
the whole brain board.

525
00:56:10,417 --> 00:56:12,000
Everything okay up there?

526
00:56:12,083 --> 00:56:13,500
Perfect.

527
00:56:20,208 --> 00:56:22,958
I told you to strap in.
Always wear your seat belt.

528
00:56:32,375 --> 00:56:34,250
Take it easy up there!

529
00:56:40,625 --> 00:56:41,958
There we go.

530
00:58:13,792 --> 00:58:15,625
That doesn't look like a Hutt.

531
00:58:15,708 --> 00:58:18,417
This is Imperial Commander
Janu Coin.

532
00:58:18,500 --> 00:58:21,667
He's full of information and
ready to sing like a Yuzzum.

533
00:58:21,750 --> 00:58:23,417
Isn't that right, Coin?

534
00:58:23,500 --> 00:58:24,917
I demand
an attorney be present

535
00:58:25,000 --> 00:58:26,167
if I'm to be questioned.

536
00:58:26,833 --> 00:58:27,833
You see?

537
00:58:28,333 --> 00:58:30,042
He's full of secrets.

538
00:58:30,875 --> 00:58:32,667
You were supposed
to bring back Rotta.

539
00:58:33,792 --> 00:58:36,042
We had an arrangement
with the Twins.

540
00:58:36,125 --> 00:58:38,208
This is your Ace of Staves.

541
00:58:38,958 --> 00:58:40,958
This is who they were
going to lead you to.

542
00:58:41,667 --> 00:58:42,792
And then tip him off,

543
00:58:42,875 --> 00:58:45,500
sell you out and collect
credits from both sides.

544
00:58:46,708 --> 00:58:48,083
Take him away.

545
00:58:53,167 --> 00:58:55,083
Intelligence
has been cultivating

546
00:58:55,167 --> 00:58:58,333
a relationship with the Hutts
for a very long time,

547
00:58:58,417 --> 00:58:59,917
and you crossed them.

548
00:59:01,375 --> 00:59:03,167
The Twins can hold a grudge.

549
00:59:03,250 --> 00:59:04,500
I made a call.

550
00:59:04,583 --> 00:59:06,208
I got you the big prize.

551
00:59:06,750 --> 00:59:08,708
The Twins can rot in hell.

552
00:59:08,792 --> 00:59:10,167
Well, you missed out
on them paying you

553
00:59:10,250 --> 00:59:12,208
a big bounty for their nephew.

554
00:59:12,292 --> 00:59:13,417
Hmm...

555
00:59:13,500 --> 00:59:14,792
So be it.

556
00:59:16,792 --> 00:59:18,833
Well, I'll see if
I can hit up Command

557
00:59:18,917 --> 00:59:20,833
for a fee
for the capture of Coin.

558
00:59:20,917 --> 00:59:23,417
Don't worry about it.
It's on me.

559
00:59:24,208 --> 00:59:25,792
This one got messy.

560
00:59:25,875 --> 00:59:27,125
I'm taking a break.

561
00:59:28,708 --> 00:59:30,042
I understand.

562
00:59:31,083 --> 00:59:32,292
Mando.

563
00:59:34,958 --> 00:59:36,208
Good job.

564
01:01:00,583 --> 01:01:02,583
We're gonna
pull the restrictor plates.

565
01:01:02,667 --> 01:01:05,333
The first one should be
just past the return line.

566
01:01:05,417 --> 01:01:06,917
That's it.

567
01:01:07,000 --> 01:01:09,125
There should be three more.

568
01:01:21,708 --> 01:01:24,000
Okay, okay. Okey-doke.

569
01:01:30,125 --> 01:01:31,125
Okay, okay.

570
01:01:31,208 --> 01:01:32,542
Thanks for coming.

571
01:01:33,208 --> 01:01:34,500
No problem.

572
01:01:34,583 --> 01:01:37,375
I'm looking to make some
performance modifications.

573
01:01:37,458 --> 01:01:39,250
I need to cut out
dead weight for speed.

574
01:01:40,667 --> 01:01:43,000
Pull out anything
that doesn't make her go.

575
01:01:43,833 --> 01:01:44,833
Hey!

576
01:01:44,917 --> 01:01:46,250
Hey. Hey.

577
01:01:46,333 --> 01:01:47,333
No, don't touch me!

578
01:01:47,417 --> 01:01:49,750
Heel.

579
01:01:49,833 --> 01:01:51,542
-The horrible baby.
-The bad baby.

580
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:53,583
Stay.

581
01:01:53,667 --> 01:01:55,000
I purged the fuel lines.

582
01:01:55,083 --> 01:01:56,750
I wanna remove
all the restrictors

583
01:01:56,833 --> 01:01:58,417
and unplug the exhaust.

584
01:01:58,500 --> 01:02:01,583
-Got it. Yeah, yeah.
-No problem. Yeah. I got it.

585
01:02:02,208 --> 01:02:03,458
-No problem.
-Yeah. Okey-doke.

586
01:02:04,917 --> 01:02:06,167
You wanna go help them?

587
01:02:08,042 --> 01:02:09,792
Do you promise to play nice?

588
01:02:11,167 --> 01:02:13,250
All right. Go.

589
01:02:19,875 --> 01:02:21,000
Don't worry about him.

590
01:02:23,375 --> 01:02:25,125
Little guy's gonna be okay.

591
01:02:27,292 --> 01:02:29,292
Sorry, I found these
in your kitchen.

592
01:02:33,125 --> 01:02:34,917
I was alone
when I was his age.

593
01:02:35,792 --> 01:02:37,333
I had to fend for myself.

594
01:02:42,708 --> 01:02:43,958
He's lucky he has you.

595
01:02:44,833 --> 01:02:47,708
Well, you didn't
turn out half bad.

596
01:02:49,125 --> 01:02:52,750
Mmm. Life's messy,
but we do the best we can.

597
01:02:54,333 --> 01:02:56,000
Listen, I called a gunrunner

598
01:02:56,083 --> 01:02:57,833
who agreed to take you
out of the system.

599
01:02:57,917 --> 01:02:59,792
We both know the Twins
will be looking for you,

600
01:02:59,875 --> 01:03:01,250
so you best keep moving.

601
01:03:26,458 --> 01:03:27,833
Thank you, Mando.

602
01:03:27,917 --> 01:03:29,375
It was a fair trade.

603
01:03:29,458 --> 01:03:31,375
Make sure you lay low.

604
01:03:31,458 --> 01:03:33,792
I don't wanna see your name
on my list again.

605
01:03:33,875 --> 01:03:35,083
You have my word.

606
01:03:36,208 --> 01:03:38,458
All right, you take care
of yourself, little guy.

607
01:03:40,000 --> 01:03:42,917
And keep an eye on
your old man, too, all right?

608
01:03:43,917 --> 01:03:45,292
Here you go.

609
01:03:45,375 --> 01:03:47,083
Hang on to these for me.

610
01:04:28,250 --> 01:04:30,583
Let's save the rest of these
for after dinner.

611
01:05:48,333 --> 01:05:50,208
Wake up.

612
01:05:50,292 --> 01:05:51,292
Oh. What? Uh.

613
01:05:51,375 --> 01:05:52,708
- Wake up.
- What's going on?

614
01:05:52,792 --> 01:05:54,042
There's someone out there.

615
01:05:54,125 --> 01:05:55,583
I'll be awake in the morning.

616
01:05:55,667 --> 01:05:57,500
Quiet. Get under the floor.

617
01:06:09,417 --> 01:06:12,708
Wait here.
If I signal, get out.

618
01:06:33,500 --> 01:06:35,875
Shh. Shh. Shh.

619
01:07:23,958 --> 01:07:27,042
Help! It got me! It got me!

620
01:07:27,125 --> 01:07:29,333
Keibu.

621
01:08:22,250 --> 01:08:24,417
Did you get the Mandalorian?

622
01:08:25,667 --> 01:08:29,458
Very good. Bring him to Nal Hutta.

623
01:08:37,542 --> 01:08:39,083
Help me! Help!

624
01:09:39,458 --> 01:09:41,667
Ow.

625
01:09:43,208 --> 01:09:45,458
Ow, ow, ow.

626
01:09:47,333 --> 01:09:48,583
Let him go.

627
01:09:55,458 --> 01:09:57,208
Hey, you hungry?

628
01:10:01,458 --> 01:10:02,958
You want a treat?

629
01:10:04,792 --> 01:10:06,208
Here you go.

630
01:10:06,292 --> 01:10:08,083
Good girl.

631
01:10:09,375 --> 01:10:10,375
Come on. Come on!

632
01:10:10,458 --> 01:10:12,500
Uh-oh.

633
01:10:12,583 --> 01:10:13,917
Oh.

634
01:10:33,625 --> 01:10:35,292
Uh-oh.

635
01:10:40,333 --> 01:10:41,958
Who hired you?

636
01:10:42,708 --> 01:10:44,167
Was it the Hutts?

637
01:10:45,708 --> 01:10:47,292
Well, if it was the Hutts,

638
01:10:47,375 --> 01:10:49,458
I'd make sure they're
paying you what you're worth.

639
01:10:49,542 --> 01:10:51,208
But I'm guessing a Kyuzo
is smart enough

640
01:10:51,292 --> 01:10:52,292
to get their money up-front--

641
01:12:49,292 --> 01:12:51,292
Nal Hutta.

642
01:12:51,375 --> 01:12:54,583
The Hutts are there.
I don't like it.

643
01:13:14,417 --> 01:13:16,208
Oh! Wow! Oh, I'm coming.

644
01:13:24,125 --> 01:13:25,333
Kid, don't be scared.

645
01:13:25,417 --> 01:13:27,167
Don't be scared.
It's okay, yeah.

646
01:13:27,250 --> 01:13:28,333
Come on, let's go.

647
01:13:28,417 --> 01:13:30,125
Oh...

648
01:13:40,542 --> 01:13:43,625
Oh! Hello!
It's me, it's me! You're here.

649
01:13:43,708 --> 01:13:46,417
You came for me! You found me!

650
01:13:47,750 --> 01:13:49,458
Oh, we thought you were dead.

651
01:13:50,417 --> 01:13:52,000
Mandalorian, he saved me.

652
01:13:52,083 --> 01:13:54,125
Big guy. He's inside there.

653
01:13:54,208 --> 01:13:56,083
Yeah, we got to go
and find him

654
01:13:56,167 --> 01:13:57,958
and bring him home
for the baby.

655
01:13:59,833 --> 01:14:02,792
The big thing. The big dog.
The big dog. The big...

656
01:14:02,875 --> 01:14:04,875
Oh, oh. It picked me up...

657
01:14:16,000 --> 01:14:18,542
Mando is in there.
In the palace.

658
01:14:31,292 --> 01:14:32,958
Come on. Up, up, up, up.

659
01:14:33,042 --> 01:14:34,875
Come on, baby. You can do it.

660
01:14:43,167 --> 01:14:44,917
Big pipe, huh?

661
01:15:13,292 --> 01:15:14,792
Good shot, baby.

662
01:15:37,042 --> 01:15:39,458
Pay the hunter.

663
01:15:55,042 --> 01:15:58,208
You broke our agreement.

664
01:15:58,292 --> 01:16:00,458
Now you must pay.

665
01:16:01,250 --> 01:16:02,917
Bring me his helmet.

666
01:16:13,000 --> 01:16:15,875
Mandalorian steel.

667
01:16:15,958 --> 01:16:19,667
Priceless on the black market.

668
01:16:21,042 --> 01:16:24,458
But worth even more is knowing

669
01:16:24,542 --> 01:16:28,250
we have shamed you forever.

670
01:16:28,875 --> 01:16:31,625
We know the Mandalorian Creed.

671
01:16:32,167 --> 01:16:33,917
You will be outcast

672
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:37,417
for letting an enemy see
your face.

673
01:16:38,083 --> 01:16:39,708
Not if you all die.

674
01:16:43,417 --> 01:16:46,792
It will bring us ecstasy

675
01:16:46,875 --> 01:16:51,708
to watch
your strong spirit break.

676
01:17:00,792 --> 01:17:01,792
Monsters.

677
01:17:02,500 --> 01:17:04,208
You did this to him.

678
01:17:04,292 --> 01:17:07,583
Rotta would have
died painlessly,

679
01:17:07,667 --> 01:17:09,083
but you betrayed us.

680
01:17:09,583 --> 01:17:13,083
Now he will suffer
for centuries.

681
01:17:13,625 --> 01:17:18,667
You see, Hutts live for
hundreds of years.

682
01:17:19,458 --> 01:17:24,000
Just like
your small, green child.

683
01:17:24,500 --> 01:17:26,583
One day you will die,

684
01:17:26,667 --> 01:17:30,542
and Grogu will be without you
to protect him.

685
01:17:30,625 --> 01:17:34,500
And then,
it will be his turn to suffer.

686
01:20:27,292 --> 01:20:29,875
You have entertained us.

687
01:20:30,667 --> 01:20:32,917
Here is your reward.

688
01:22:31,917 --> 01:22:33,917
Uh-oh. Which way?

689
01:23:38,458 --> 01:23:42,167
Even if
you win, you will die from the poison.

690
01:24:08,292 --> 01:24:09,417
Dank farrik.

691
01:24:12,750 --> 01:24:14,000
Get out! Go!

692
01:24:16,125 --> 01:24:18,125
Come on, go! Go, go!

693
01:24:32,667 --> 01:24:35,500
-Oh, yeah!
-Wow!

694
01:24:35,583 --> 01:24:36,958
Wait. Wait.

695
01:25:05,375 --> 01:25:07,042
You okay?

696
01:25:13,000 --> 01:25:15,417
-How did you get here?
-We got a ship.

697
01:25:15,500 --> 01:25:16,958
That way. Let's go!

698
01:25:23,583 --> 01:25:27,333
Send the droids!
Release the Amani! Don't let him escape!

699
01:25:53,000 --> 01:25:54,792
This way. This way, yeah.

700
01:26:06,875 --> 01:26:08,667
This way!

701
01:26:15,083 --> 01:26:16,833
Up, up, up, up, going up!

702
01:26:16,917 --> 01:26:18,833
I don't want to fall.
I don't want to.

703
01:26:19,542 --> 01:26:20,542
Go!

704
01:26:20,625 --> 01:26:22,750
Yeah. Okay, okay. Yeah.
Let's go.

705
01:26:35,583 --> 01:26:37,958
Go, kid.
I can't fit in that thing,

706
01:26:39,250 --> 01:26:41,000
but you have to leave.

707
01:26:43,542 --> 01:26:44,750
Don't worry.

708
01:26:45,375 --> 01:26:47,083
I'll be right behind you.

709
01:26:51,250 --> 01:26:53,667
Go now. I'll hold them off.

710
01:26:54,208 --> 01:26:56,125
We'll come back
for you, Mando.

711
01:26:59,958 --> 01:27:01,208
Come on, baby.

712
01:27:01,292 --> 01:27:03,167
Don't worry. We'll be back.

713
01:27:03,250 --> 01:27:05,500
Yeah, let's go. Let's go.

714
01:27:05,583 --> 01:27:06,750
Come on, baby.

715
01:28:37,667 --> 01:28:39,042
Goodbye, kid.

716
01:31:33,042 --> 01:31:34,833
No life force detected.

717
01:37:32,417 --> 01:37:35,125
Methinks you are
the one who stole my fish.

718
01:37:49,208 --> 01:37:51,875
I'm guessing
you're not from around here.

719
01:37:55,833 --> 01:37:58,833
A morsel like you
should be more careful.

720
01:37:58,917 --> 01:38:02,417
You look to be the bottom
of the Nal Hutta food chain.

721
01:38:03,917 --> 01:38:05,958
I'm surprised
you haven't found your way

722
01:38:06,042 --> 01:38:07,792
to the Hutts' supper table.

723
01:38:10,375 --> 01:38:12,208
You've heard of the Hutts,
have you?

724
01:38:13,417 --> 01:38:14,667
Are you scared?

725
01:38:16,458 --> 01:38:17,583
You should be.

726
01:38:18,083 --> 01:38:21,042
They would swallow you whole
given half a chance.

727
01:38:25,542 --> 01:38:27,333
Make yourself scarce.

728
01:38:50,167 --> 01:38:51,125
Uh-huh.

729
01:39:26,125 --> 01:39:27,292
Hey.

730
01:39:29,167 --> 01:39:30,583
Get away from my fish.

731
01:39:35,792 --> 01:39:37,417
Keibu.

732
01:39:58,000 --> 01:40:00,000
The hunter says
you have a partner.

733
01:40:01,625 --> 01:40:04,542
Says you two
escaped the Twins.

734
01:40:04,625 --> 01:40:06,500
Well, that's impressive.

735
01:40:12,167 --> 01:40:14,875
Says your partner's
hurt real bad.

736
01:40:14,958 --> 01:40:18,208
Bit by a dragonsnake.
Poisoned.

737
01:40:22,375 --> 01:40:24,667
I want you
to feed this to him.

738
01:40:26,958 --> 01:40:27,958
Now, you should know,

739
01:40:28,042 --> 01:40:30,125
this might be too little,
too late,

740
01:40:30,625 --> 01:40:33,375
and there's a good chance
he doesn't wake up.

741
01:40:37,792 --> 01:40:39,792
Either way,
best thing you can do

742
01:40:39,875 --> 01:40:41,458
right now
is make him comfortable.

743
01:40:42,417 --> 01:40:45,583
There comes a time where
we all have to say goodbye.

744
01:40:52,833 --> 01:40:55,250
I wish you luck,
small traveler.

745
01:43:43,000 --> 01:43:44,042
Hey, kiddo.

746
01:43:49,833 --> 01:43:51,167
The old protect the young,

747
01:43:51,250 --> 01:43:53,042
and then the young
protect the old.

748
01:43:54,167 --> 01:43:55,500
This is the Way.

749
01:43:58,667 --> 01:44:00,333
Now how do we
get off this planet?

750
01:44:07,500 --> 01:44:10,042
That's the gunrunner
that was carrying Rotta.

751
01:46:24,708 --> 01:46:28,417
Well, kid, the way I see it
we got two choices.

752
01:46:29,125 --> 01:46:31,583
We can use this ship.
Get off world.

753
01:46:32,250 --> 01:46:34,750
That might buy us some time.
A little bit of peace.

754
01:46:35,250 --> 01:46:37,458
But the Hutts
will keep coming for us.

755
01:46:38,542 --> 01:46:40,292
Just like they came for Rotta.

756
01:46:43,417 --> 01:46:44,500
So, do we run?

757
01:46:48,792 --> 01:46:49,875
Or do we fight?

758
01:47:33,875 --> 01:47:35,667
Huh?

759
01:47:51,583 --> 01:47:53,375
Repel the intruders!

760
01:47:53,458 --> 01:47:54,958
Roger, roger!

761
01:47:55,625 --> 01:47:57,042
Protect the palace!

762
01:47:57,125 --> 01:47:58,042
Affirmative.

763
01:48:07,583 --> 01:48:08,708
Follow my lead.

764
01:48:13,125 --> 01:48:14,208
Fire!

765
01:48:25,167 --> 01:48:26,750
Come on. Come on.

766
01:49:05,500 --> 01:49:07,042
On me.

767
01:49:50,708 --> 01:49:51,708
Fall back!

768
01:52:28,250 --> 01:52:30,333
Wait! We know much.

769
01:52:30,417 --> 01:52:31,917
Go help Rotta.

770
01:52:40,125 --> 01:52:41,667
You saw my face.

771
01:52:42,583 --> 01:52:43,333
Stop!

772
01:52:44,333 --> 01:52:45,833
Now it's time to die.

773
01:53:54,875 --> 01:53:55,958
Leave him alone!

774
01:54:18,125 --> 01:54:20,917
You don't have Jabba to protect you.

775
01:54:21,500 --> 01:54:22,958
I'm not little anymore!

776
01:55:54,208 --> 01:55:57,458
Stop! You'll kill us all!

777
01:56:42,000 --> 01:56:43,542
Save us, bounty hunter!

778
01:56:44,917 --> 01:56:45,917
Keibu.

779
01:56:46,000 --> 01:56:47,667
Save us!

780
01:57:22,000 --> 01:57:24,667
We don't have much time.
We have to get out of here.

781
01:57:25,625 --> 01:57:26,833
Is there another way out?

782
01:57:26,917 --> 01:57:29,583
-I think it's that way.
-Go. Go!

783
01:57:46,083 --> 01:57:47,000
Target sighted.

784
01:58:13,000 --> 01:58:13,917
Hello?

785
01:58:14,000 --> 01:58:15,875
Mando! We came back.

786
01:58:15,958 --> 01:58:17,208
-What?
-We came back.

787
01:58:17,292 --> 01:58:19,000
We told you we would.

788
01:58:26,042 --> 01:58:29,000
Adelphi Squadron,
entering atmosphere.

789
01:58:29,958 --> 01:58:32,667
-What's your status, Mando?
-We're under attack.

790
01:58:33,667 --> 01:58:35,000
There are too many.

791
01:58:35,083 --> 01:58:37,083
Fire everything you have
at my location.

792
01:58:38,625 --> 01:58:41,833
- Your location?
- Yes, my location.

793
01:58:41,917 --> 01:58:43,417
I can't give that order.

794
01:58:43,500 --> 01:58:44,917
Don't worry...

795
01:58:46,917 --> 01:58:49,125
we'll be out of here
by the time you do.

796
01:58:50,750 --> 01:58:51,792
Good luck.

797
01:58:55,375 --> 01:58:56,667
Blue Leader to squadron,

798
01:58:57,250 --> 01:59:00,292
assume defensive formation,
prepare to engage.

799
01:59:00,375 --> 01:59:01,542
All weapons hot.

800
01:59:01,625 --> 01:59:02,458
Copy that.

801
01:59:20,083 --> 01:59:21,833
Enemy fighters approaching.

802
01:59:24,000 --> 01:59:24,875
Here they come.

803
01:59:52,167 --> 01:59:53,500
Turbolasers, up ahead.

804
01:59:53,583 --> 01:59:54,750
Got it.

805
02:00:15,625 --> 02:00:17,042
I've got one on my tail.

806
02:00:19,750 --> 02:00:21,250
I got you.

807
02:00:31,417 --> 02:00:33,042
Yippee! Yay!

808
02:00:33,125 --> 02:00:34,708
Taking out the launch tubes.

809
02:00:42,458 --> 02:00:45,333
Blue Leader to Red Jammer,
mark it and lock it in.

810
02:00:47,833 --> 02:00:48,958
Locking in target.

811
02:00:52,667 --> 02:00:53,708
It's a dead end.

812
02:00:55,000 --> 02:00:56,417
We're trapped.

813
02:00:57,125 --> 02:00:58,333
Stand back.

814
02:01:04,708 --> 02:01:06,042
We're closing fast.

815
02:01:06,125 --> 02:01:07,542
Repeat, we're closing fast.

816
02:01:07,625 --> 02:01:09,208
You better be
out of there, Mando.

817
02:01:09,292 --> 02:01:10,708
Jump.

818
02:01:10,792 --> 02:01:12,875
That's a long way down.

819
02:01:12,958 --> 02:01:14,167
Closing on target.

820
02:01:15,708 --> 02:01:18,000
- Gotta jump.
- Moat's not that deep.

821
02:01:18,083 --> 02:01:20,125
It's a bomber. Jump.

822
02:01:20,208 --> 02:01:22,000
Let's light up this swamp.

823
02:01:56,792 --> 02:01:58,417
Anybody got eyes on Mando?

824
02:01:59,083 --> 02:02:00,083
There they are.

825
02:02:04,500 --> 02:02:08,250
Zeb, go collect the trash.

826
02:02:16,375 --> 02:02:19,167
I'm getting a little tired
of these hot extractions.

827
02:02:20,083 --> 02:02:22,042
What took you so long?

828
02:02:23,375 --> 02:02:24,500
Hop in.

829
02:02:24,583 --> 02:02:26,417
Let's head home.

830
02:02:49,333 --> 02:02:50,708
Colonel.

831
02:02:53,042 --> 02:02:54,417
Messy.

832
02:02:55,000 --> 02:02:56,250
Very messy.

833
02:02:57,458 --> 02:02:59,083
Why'd you come for me?

834
02:02:59,167 --> 02:03:00,667
That wasn't part
of the mission.

835
02:03:01,417 --> 02:03:04,542
You were right.
Coin told us everything.

836
02:03:05,042 --> 02:03:06,667
The Twins were playing us.

837
02:03:06,750 --> 02:03:09,292
Feeding information
to the Empire all along.

838
02:03:10,625 --> 02:03:13,292
They picked a side.
It wasn't ours.

839
02:03:13,917 --> 02:03:17,542
Besides,
we don't leave our own behind.

840
02:03:18,083 --> 02:03:19,875
I'm an independent contractor.

841
02:03:19,958 --> 02:03:22,917
Sure, Mando. Sure you are.

842
02:03:33,583 --> 02:03:35,500
Can I give you a ride
somewhere?

843
02:03:35,583 --> 02:03:37,792
Actually, I was thinking
I could stay here.

844
02:03:38,583 --> 02:03:40,375
Maybe work
for the New Republic.

845
02:03:40,958 --> 02:03:43,375
Don't take this
the wrong way, but...

846
02:03:43,458 --> 02:03:45,542
I'm not sure you would fit in.

847
02:03:45,625 --> 02:03:47,458
You know...

848
02:03:47,542 --> 02:03:49,792
...I might have
a uniform that would fit him.

849
02:03:50,833 --> 02:03:53,708
Come on,
let me buy you a drink.

850
02:03:55,500 --> 02:03:58,042
Thank you, Mando.
I owe you big time.

851
02:03:58,125 --> 02:03:59,458
Just doing my job.

852
02:04:00,083 --> 02:04:01,083
And keep an eye on him.

853
02:04:02,208 --> 02:04:03,833
Your dad's
one of the good ones.

854
02:04:18,292 --> 02:04:19,583
Come on, big guy.

855
02:04:20,750 --> 02:04:23,125
Watch your step.
First round's on me.

856
02:04:32,292 --> 02:04:34,417
Hey, kid. Come up here.

857
02:04:54,083 --> 02:04:55,292
Your turn.

858
02:04:58,208 --> 02:04:59,208
Go ahead.